## 4.4 Consequences of Attendance Shortage  
A student whose attendance is below the minimum and who has not been granted condonation receives grade DT in that course. A DT student:  
- may not sit the final examination (or practical examination) of that course;  
- is not eligible for a supplementary examination in that course, because supplementary examinations are available only to students who were eligible for the final examination (?? of the Examination Guidelines);  
- must re-register for the course when it is next offered and pay the re-registration charge (see Section 5.5);  
- is treated as having failed the course for the purpose of scholarship eligibility (see Scholarship Guidelines (NIT-SG-2026)).  
NOTE Detention does not count as an examination attempt. Examination attendance eligibility is also described in ?? of the Examination Guidelines, which applies the thresholds defined here.
